    "result_text": "All 34 tests pass, including the new `Cp23Tests` (GOLD) and the existing `Cp15Tests` (SILVER/BRONZE) \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe membership tier is derived by `OwnerMapper` from fields snapshotted onto the `Owner` at create time (this is how the existing SILVER/BRONZE rule already works via `namesakeCount`). I extended that same pattern for GOLD:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `householdMemberCount` field with getter/setter (mirrors `namesakeCount`).\n\n2. **`AssignHouseholdMemberCount.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners sharing the built owner's `householdId`, plus one for the owner being created (which isn't saved yet at this pipeline stage). No `householdId` (didn't opt into a shared household) \u21d2 count of 1.\n\n3. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the pipeline right after `assignHousehold` (which assigns/back-fills the shared `householdId`) and before `assignCustomerCode`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 tier expression now checks GOLD first (`householdMemberCount >= 3`), falling back to the unchanged SILVER/BRONZE logic.\n\n5. **Schema files** (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres) \u2014 added the `household_member_count` column, and updated the `membershipTier` description in `openapi.yml`.\n\nFor the test's three-member shared household, the third create sees the two already-saved members plus itself = 3 \u21d2 GOLD, while the earlier members keep their snapshot as-created \u2014 consistent with \"3+ members *after this create*.\"",
